WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:11.543
In tutorial 8.9, you'll bring in your
AI reports from Bing and Search Console.

00:00:12.583 --> 00:00:16.408
First, scroll down AI
visibility to Your AI reports,

00:00:16.458 --> 00:00:20.096
for Copilot's citations and
Google's AI search figures.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.699
Click Show me how for a
guide to both exports.

00:00:25.594 --> 00:00:29.694
In Bing Webmaster Tools, open
AI Performance, pick a period,

00:00:29.744 --> 00:00:32.295
and export the table as a CSV file.

00:00:33.293 --> 00:00:37.843
In Search Console, filter Performance
to AI Overviews or AI Mode,

00:00:37.893 --> 00:00:40.634
where it's offered, and download the CSV.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:47.409
Leave Report on Recognise it from the file,
click Upload a CSV, and choose the file.

00:00:47.459 --> 00:00:49.317
A message shows what it read.

00:00:50.257 --> 00:00:53.057
A Queries or Pages file has no dates,

00:00:53.107 --> 00:00:56.348
so first choose the report and
the last day of the period.

00:00:57.325 --> 00:01:00.375
After the upload, check
the top searches it shows,

00:01:00.425 --> 00:01:02.618
to be sure the file is for your website.

00:01:03.548 --> 00:01:08.023
Your AI reports now lists each
upload, with its days, citations,

00:01:08.073 --> 00:01:11.025
impressions and clicks,
for your next weekly check.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:16.836
So Bing's and Google's AI figures sit
right beside your own AI visibility.

00:01:17.824 --> 00:01:23.159
So, open Your AI reports, export from
Bing and Search Console, upload the file,

00:01:23.209 --> 00:01:24.465
and read what it adds.

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:31.119
Now your AI reports are in. Next,
choose extra AI checks in tutorial 8.10.
